    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0536" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg440"/>

                <head>No. 255.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Bancroft.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-02-11"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 11,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 648.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 562, of the 16th
                    ultimo, relating to the final denial by the proper authorities of reports
                    concerning negotiations between Germany and Denmark respecting the cession of
                    the Danish West Indies, I have to request you to be watchful in case any
                    negotiation of that character should occur.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
